其中一个是把 Python 迁移到那个庞大的 Facebook 单体代码库上
So one was migrating from Python to the big Facebook monolith.

361
00:16:00,810 --> 00:16:02,510
另一个是从 Rust 迁移到 GraphQL
Another one was migrating from Rust to GraphQL.

362
00:16:03,490 --> 00:16:05,570
这些项目其实现在都还在进行中
And these projects, they're actually in progress.

363
00:16:05,770 --> 00:16:07,530
你也知道，这类事情往往意味着
You know, like these are things that involve...

364
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:09,670
需要几百名工程师花上好几年才能搞定
It takes hundreds of engineers many years to do this.

365
00:16:10,030 --> 00:16:10,710
代码库非常庞大
It's a big code base.

366
00:16:10,790 --> 00:16:11,390
迁移工程也非常巨大
It's a big migration.

367
00:16:12,650 --> 00:16:14,110
现在要快得多了
Now it's much faster.

368
00:16:14,570 --> 00:16:17,650
是的，多亏了我们现在有的这些 AI 工具
Yeah, with these tools that we have, the AI tools.

369
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:20,010
而迁移本身就是一个非常适合它们的用例
And migrations are a pretty good use case for them though.

370
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:22,250
对，这几乎是它们的完美用例
Yeah, it's like the perfect use case for it.

371
00:16:22,410 --> 00:16:24,830
然后我就开始更深入地投入到这块工作里
And then I just started getting kind of deeper into this.

372
00:16:24,990 --> 00:16:26,670
到后来、也就是我离开 Instagram 的时候
And by the end, by the time I left Instagram,

373
00:16:26,790 --> 00:16:29,890
我一直在做开发基础设施，并负责领导其中一大批迁移项目
so I was working on this on DevInfra and kind of leading a bunch of these migrations.

374
00:16:30,410 --> 00:16:32,370
也是在那时候，我和 Fiona Fung 有了交集
That's also where I intersected with Fiona Fung,

375
00:16:32,850 --> 00:16:35,070
她现在是 Claude Code 团队的经理
who is now the manager for the Claude Code team.

376
00:16:35,310 --> 00:16:37,650
我当时和她一起工作，发现她真的是一位非常出色的领导者
I just worked with her and she was just such an amazing leader.

377
00:16:37,930 --> 00:16:40,230
在技术上有着惊人的深度和丰富的从业经历
This incredible depth and kind of history in tech.

378
00:16:40,230 --> 00:16:44,010
我当时就觉得，这个团队不可能有比她更合适的经理了
And I just thought there's no better manager for this team.

379
00:16:44,290 --> 00:16:46,210
后来我也开始做代码质量相关的工作
And then I also started working on code quality.

380
00:16:47,270 --> 00:16:49,430
所以我在 Instagram 的工作范围也随之扩大了一些
And so the work on Instagram kind of expanded a bit.

381
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:51,810
等到我离开的时候
And by the time I left,

382
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:53,610
我已经在负责整个 Meta 的代码质量
I was leading code quality for all of Meta.

383
00:16:54,190 --> 00:16:59,630
也就是说，我要对 Instagram、Facebook、Messenger、WhatsApp
And so I was responsible for the quality of the code bases across Instagram, Facebook, Messenger, WhatsApp,

384
00:16:59,910 --> 00:17:01,970
Reality Labs 等所有这些代码库的质量负责
Reality Labs, kind of all these code bases.

385
00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:04,250
在 Meta，这个项目叫做“Better Engineering”
At Meta, it was this program called Better Engineering.

386
00:17:05,050 --> 00:17:08,750
这个想法大概是在 2016 或 2018 年左右提出的
And the idea was, I think it's sort of like 2016 or 2018 or something.

387
00:17:08,750 --> 00:17:12,050
当时扎克伯格要求公司里的每一位工程师
But Zuck mandated that every engineer at the company,

388
00:17:12,410 --> 00:17:15,550
必须拿出 20% 的时间来修复技术债务
20% of their time has to be spent fixing tech debt.

389
00:17:16,590 --> 00:17:18,930
挺有意思的，我们把这项计划称为 Better Engineering
Oh, interesting. And we called this Better Engineering.

390
00:17:20,710 --> 00:17:22,670
其中一部分是自下而上的
And some of this is kind of bottom-up,

391
00:17:22,850 --> 00:17:26,150
团队自己最清楚该修哪些技术债
where a team knows best the tech debt that they have to fix.

392
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:27,190
还有一部分是自上而下的
And then some of it is top-down,

393
00:17:27,630 --> 00:17:29,990
比如你需要做非常大规模的迁移
where you need to do very big migrations.

394
00:17:30,190 --> 00:17:32,210
需要迁移到新的语言特性
You need to migrate to new language features,

395
00:17:32,390 --> 00:17:33,790
新的框架之类的东西
new frameworks, things like this.

396
00:17:34,310 --> 00:17:35,310
而在 Facebook 这种体量下
And at Facebook scale,

397
00:17:35,690 --> 00:17:37,870
每年都有成千上万次这样的迁移
there was tens of thousands of these migrations every year.

398
00:17:38,750 --> 00:17:40,730
所以我就开始主导所有这些事情
And so I just started leading all this.

399
00:17:40,910 --> 00:17:44,910
我很快就意识到你只需要给这件事多加一点秩序
And I realized very quick that you just need a little bit more order to it.

400
00:17:45,050 --> 00:17:45,870
当时没有任何目标
There was no goals.

401
00:17:46,150 --> 00:17:47,690
没有人大致知道预期结果是什么
No one knew kind of like what the outcomes were.

402
00:17:47,890 --> 00:17:48,950
也没有任何跟踪记录
There wasn't any tracking.

403
00:17:50,170 --> 00:17:51,750
所以我们开发了一堆东西
And so we developed a bunch of stuff.

404
00:17:52,390 --> 00:17:57,630
其中一个想法是用一种集中化的方式来给不同类型的代码质量工作排优先级
One of the ideas was a centralized way to prioritize the different kind of code quality efforts.

405
00:17:57,890 --> 00:18:01,150
第二件事是弄清楚代码质量对工程效率的影响
The second thing was figuring out the impact of code quality on engineering productivity,

406
00:18:01,150 --> 00:18:02,410
结果发现影响非常大
which turned out to be significant.

407
00:18:03,330 --> 00:18:04,130
你们是怎么衡量的
How did you measure?

408
00:18:04,210 --> 00:18:04,870
你们在那里发现了什么
What did you find there?

409
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:06,090
有很多发现
There was a bunch of stuff.

410
00:18:06,170 --> 00:18:07,410
我想其中一部分已经发表过
I think some of this has been published.

411
00:18:07,410 --> 00:18:08,830
我不确定是不是全部都发表了
I don't know if all of it has.

412
00:18:09,010 --> 00:18:12,250
但本质上你会尝试做因果分析和因果推断
But essentially, you try to do causal analysis and causal inference.

413
00:18:12,470 --> 00:18:13,250
这就是方法论
This is the methodology.

414
00:18:14,290 --> 00:18:17,490
你会试着找出哪些因素能让工程师更高效
You try to figure out what are the factors that make it so engineers are more productive.

415
00:18:17,950 --> 00:18:18,850
其中一部分是代码质量
Some of it is code quality.

416
00:18:18,950 --> 00:18:20,350
还有一部分是代码质量之外的因素
Some of it is outside of code quality.

417
00:18:20,670 --> 00:18:24,730
比如说 Meta 从在家办公改回了回办公室上班
So for example, Meta went back to return to office instead of work from home.

418
00:18:25,050 --> 00:18:26,190
这在一定程度上就是被这些结果推动的
It was partially driven by this.

419
00:18:26,570 --> 00:18:31,510
因为我们发现了一些相当强的相关性并认为在这件事上是因果关系
Because we just found some fairly strong correlations that we thought were causal about this.

420
00:18:31,750 --> 00:18:35,430
但代码质量对生产力的贡献实际上是两位数百分比
But code quality actually contributes double digit percent to productivity.

421
00:18:35,430 --> 00:18:37,890
事实证明即使在最大规模下也是如此
It turns out, even at the biggest scale.

422
00:18:38,550 --> 00:18:39,770
听到这个还是挺让人安心的
It's kind of comforting to hear.

423
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:44,010
因为我觉得很少有地方真的会去衡量这些东西
Because I think it's rare to have a place where you actually measure this.

424
00:18:44,070 --> 00:18:45,050
但我觉得我们是能感受到的
But I think we feel it.

425
00:18:45,150 --> 00:18:46,790
比如当你有一个干净的代码库时
Like when you have a clean code base,

426
00:18:46,910 --> 00:18:49,810
模块化良好或者说更容易使用
modular, or it can get easier to work with.

427
00:18:49,930 --> 00:18:50,990
而且我觉得你知道
And I think, you know,

428
00:18:51,430 --> 00:18:55,490
从推理角度看这是不是也会让大模型更容易处理它
reasoning, could it also be easier for LLMs to work with it?

429
00:18:55,590 --> 00:18:57,250
我的直觉是
And my hint would be,

430
00:18:57,450 --> 00:18:59,070
是的应该会对吧
yes, it should be, right?

431
00:18:59,390 --> 00:19:01,210
但我觉得目前几乎没有什么数据
But I think there's just very little data.

432
00:19:01,290 --> 00:19:03,070
但这是我个人的感觉
But that's the feeling that I would have.

433
00:19:03,070 --> 00:19:05,770
是的我觉得很多大公司都发表过相关内容
Yeah, I think a lot of the big companies have published about this.

434
00:19:05,970 --> 00:19:07,390
我记得 Facebook 发过一些东西
I think Facebook published something.

435
00:19:08,190 --> 00:19:09,530
微软在这方面发表了很多
Microsoft publishes a bunch about this.

436
00:19:09,590 --> 00:19:11,070
Google 也有但对完全是这样
Google does. But yeah, totally.

437
00:19:11,490 --> 00:19:13,330
如果你每次做一个新功能
If every time that you build a feature,

438
00:19:13,910 --> 00:19:16,830
你得想一想，我该用框架X还是Y还是Z
you have to think about, do I use framework X or Y or Z?

439
00:19:17,290 --> 00:19:19,130
这些都是你得考虑的选项
These are all options that you can consider.

440
00:19:19,250 --> 00:19:21,610
因为代码库处在一个只迁移了一部分的状态
Because the code base is in a partially migrated state.

441
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:23,790
这些东西都在代码的某个角落里
Where all of these are around the code somewhere.

442
00:19:24,370 --> 00:19:26,130
作为工程师你会过得很痛苦
As an engineer, you're going to have a bad time.

443
00:19:26,270 --> 00:19:27,790
作为新员工你会过得很痛苦
As a new hire, you're going to have a bad time.

444
00:19:28,210 --> 00:19:30,230
作为一个模型你可能就会选错东西
As a model, you might just pick the wrong thing.

445
00:19:30,610 --> 00:19:32,550
然后你知道用户就得不断帮你纠正
And then, you know, the user has to of course correct you.

446
00:19:32,550 --> 00:19:33,470
所以其实你知道
So actually, you know,

447
00:19:33,530 --> 00:19:37,170
更好的做法就是始终保持一个干净的代码库
the better thing to do is just always have a clean code base.

448
00:19:37,570 --> 00:19:39,650
一定要确保当你开始一次迁移时
Always make sure that when you start a migration,

449
00:19:39,870 --> 00:19:40,850
你会把这次迁移做完
you finish the migration.

