要怎么确保如果公司里有一个作恶的 IT 人员
How do we make sure that if there's a rogue IT person within the company,

1204
00:51:28,170 --> 00:51:29,630
他也不能访问别人的数据
they can't access someone else's data?

1205
00:51:29,890 --> 00:51:32,050
这一点真的非常非常重要 我们必须认真考虑
This is really, really important that we think about this.

1206
00:51:33,070 --> 00:51:36,050
所以我们最后觉得 这个方案虽然勉强能用
And so we just decided it was sort of working,

1207
00:51:36,170 --> 00:51:38,170
但缺点实在太多
but it also has a lot of downsides.

1208
00:51:38,250 --> 00:51:40,090
于是我们又尝试了一堆别的方案
So we tried a bunch of other stuff.

1209
00:51:40,630 --> 00:51:44,630
其中一个就是直接用模型递归式地给所有东西建索引
One of them was just using the model to kind of index everything recursively.

1210
00:51:45,110 --> 00:51:46,250
这个想法本身还挺酷的
That was kind of a cool idea.

1211
00:51:46,530 --> 00:51:50,030
还有一个版本是我们直接用 glob 和 grep
There was another version where we just tried glob and grep.

1212
00:51:50,230 --> 00:51:51,330
我们试了很多不同的办法
We tried a bunch of different stuff.

1213
00:51:51,490 --> 00:51:53,850
结果发现 agentic search 的效果远胜其他所有方案
It turned out that agentic search just outperformed everything.

1214
00:51:54,830 --> 00:51:56,170
我说的 agentic search
And when I say agentic search,

1215
00:51:56,790 --> 00:51:58,190
其实就是给 glob 和 grep 起了个高级点的名字
it's a fancy word for glob and grep.

1216
00:51:58,570 --> 00:51:59,190
就仅此而已
That's all it is.

1217
00:51:59,570 --> 00:52:02,450
不错 所以一方面模型本身已经足够强
Nice. So the model both got good enough,

1218
00:52:02,470 --> 00:52:05,010
另一方面你们也意识到它可以非常高效地使用这些工具
and you realize that they can use these tools pretty efficiently.

1219
00:52:05,010 --> 00:52:08,130
对 而且这部分灵感其实来自
Yeah, and this was partially inspired,

1220
00:52:08,290 --> 00:52:09,670
说实话 来自我在 Instagram 的经历
honestly, by my experience at Instagram.

1221
00:52:10,370 --> 00:52:15,830
因为在 Instagram 里 点击跳转到定义基本是废的 开发栈有一半时间都是坏的
Because at Instagram, click-to-definition didn't work because the dev stack was just borked like half the time.

1222
00:52:16,470 --> 00:52:17,490
我觉得现在应该好一些了
And I think now it's better.

1223
00:52:18,170 --> 00:52:21,070
所以工程师们学会的替代做法是
And so what engineers learned to do instead is,

1224
00:52:21,330 --> 00:52:23,550
比如你在找函数 foo 的定义
let's say you're looking for the definition of the function foo.

1225
00:52:24,090 --> 00:52:27,610
你不会点跳转到定义 而是用全局索引
Instead of click-to-definition, what you would do is you would use the global index,

1226
00:52:27,690 --> 00:52:28,670
在 Meta 这块做得其实挺好
which is quite good at meta,

1227
00:52:28,990 --> 00:52:31,370
然后搜索“foo(”这个模式
and then you would search for foo per opening parenthesis.

1228
00:52:31,790 --> 00:52:33,530
这样效果相当不错
And this worked pretty well.

1229
00:52:34,170 --> 00:52:38,050
有意思的是 对模型来说 这种方法也很好用
And it's funny, because this works for the model pretty well, too.

1230
00:52:38,710 --> 00:52:42,430
挺有意思的 一个领域里的点子可以迁移到另一个领域
Interesting how one idea from one area can come to the other.

1231
00:52:42,810 --> 00:52:49,090
我们之前也提到过 Claude Code 里一个比较高级的部分 就是权限系统
One of the more advanced parts of Claude Code that we also previously talked about is the permission system.

1232
00:52:50,070 --> 00:52:53,530
你能讲讲它复杂在哪里吗
Can you talk about what was complex about it?

1233
00:52:53,830 --> 00:52:56,510
还有 你们最近把沙箱开源了 对吧
And also, you recently opened source sandboxing, right?

1234
00:52:56,950 --> 00:52:58,290
权限控制这块真的非常复杂
Permissioning is really complex.

1235
00:52:59,570 --> 00:53:02,650
里面牵扯到所有和安全相关的东西
There's everything else that has to do with security.

1236
00:53:02,650 --> 00:53:05,030
它更像是一个瑞士奶酪模型
It's a Swiss cheese model.

1237
00:53:05,290 --> 00:53:09,290
我们会跑一系列分类器来确保命令是安全的
There are a number of classifiers that run to make sure the command is safe.

1238
00:53:10,290 --> 00:53:13,510
还会做静态分析来进一步确认命令是安全的
And there's also static analysis that we do to make sure the command is safe.

1239
00:53:14,030 --> 00:53:17,750
作为用户 你也可以把你确信安全的特定模式加入允许列表
As a user, you can also allow list particular patterns that you know to be safe.

1240
00:53:18,290 --> 00:53:22,430
比如说 一些标准的 Unix 工具我们会预先允许
So for example, some standard Unix utilities we pre-allow,

1241
00:53:22,670 --> 00:53:23,950
因为我们知道它们是只读的
because we know they're read-only,

1242
00:53:24,170 --> 00:53:26,470
也知道它们没法导出你的数据之类的
because we know they can't export your data or anything like this.

1243
00:53:26,750 --> 00:53:29,010
所以我们就不会再弹权限确认
So we just won't prompt you for permission.

1244
00:53:29,010 --> 00:53:32,990
但实际上 真正能归到这一类的工具非常少
But actually, quite few tools fall into this category.

1245
00:53:33,590 --> 00:53:35,570
因为就算是 find 这种命令
Because even something like the find command,

1246
00:53:35,970 --> 00:53:39,230
其实也有办法在命令里执行任意代码
there's actually a way to execute arbitrary code as part of that command.

1247
00:53:39,570 --> 00:53:41,990
因为有一些系统级的标志可以这么用
Because there's system flags that you can use for this.

1248
00:53:42,230 --> 00:53:43,630
甚至像 sed 这样的命令
Or even something like the sed command,

1249
00:53:43,710 --> 00:53:44,610
也有类似的用法
there's ways to use this.

1250
00:53:44,970 --> 00:53:49,850
所以围绕这些 Unix 工具有一大堆非常晦涩的细节 实际上
So there's just all this arcania about these various Unix utilities where it's actually

1251
00:53:49,850 --> 00:53:50,830
它们远没有你想的那么安全
not as safe as you think.

1252
00:53:51,470 --> 00:53:52,170
所以我们希望在这方面
And so we want to be,

1253
00:53:52,310 --> 00:53:55,450
默认情况下对允许的内容保持相当保守
by default, fairly conservative about what we allow by default.

1254
00:53:55,710 --> 00:53:57,710
不过作为用户 你可以自己配置一个允许列表
As a user, though, you can configure an allow list.

1255
00:53:57,710 --> 00:53:58,730
比如你可以指定
So you can say, for example,

1256
00:53:58,850 --> 00:53:59,970
这些模式是允许的
these patterns are allowed,

1257
00:54:00,090 --> 00:54:01,410
这些模式是不允许的
these patterns are not allowed.

1258
00:54:02,110 --> 00:54:03,610
我们允许你自己定义这些规则
And so we let you define that,

1259
00:54:03,690 --> 00:54:06,850
然后我们也会检查这个允许列表 以确保它本身是安全的
and we also check this allow list to make sure that it's safe.

1260
00:54:07,810 --> 00:54:13,750
对 然后你们还有一个很巧妙的权限系统 每次运行需要授权的命令时
Yeah, and then you have this neat permission system where every time you run a command that needs permission,

1261
00:54:13,830 --> 00:54:15,070
你可以选择只运行这一次
you can decide to run it once,

1262
00:54:15,490 --> 00:54:17,570
或者在当前会话内都允许运行
or run it for either this session,

1263
00:54:17,710 --> 00:54:18,710
或者用其他你觉得合适的范围
or whatever it makes sense,

1264
00:54:18,810 --> 00:54:21,170
甚至可以选择之后全局都允许 对吧
or just globally allowed going forward, right?

1265
00:54:21,410 --> 00:54:23,310
对 这是个挺有意思的“遗留物”
That's right. This is a funny artifact.

1266
00:54:23,430 --> 00:54:24,350
这个设计其实在非常
This was actually in the very,

1267
00:54:24,430 --> 00:54:25,870
非常早期的 Claude Code 第一个版本里就有了
very first version of Claude Code.

1268
00:54:25,870 --> 00:54:27,630
当时权限就是这么运作的
This is the way permissions worked.

1269
00:54:27,870 --> 00:54:29,070
那是最初的第一个发布版本
This is the very first release.

1270
00:54:29,170 --> 00:54:30,750
大概是在 2024 年 9 月
This was like September 2024,

1271
00:54:31,490 --> 00:54:32,590
第一个内部发布
the first internal release.

1272
00:54:32,890 --> 00:54:36,910
我记得当时我们都不确定 agentic safety 这种问题是不是根本就无解
I remember at the time we weren't sure whether agentic safety could even be solved.

1273
00:54:37,890 --> 00:54:40,810
所以安全团队内部其实有很多反对意见 因为他们觉得
And so there was actually a lot of pushback internally from safety teams because they were

1274
00:54:40,810 --> 00:54:44,690
你不能就这么让模型随便跑 bash 命令
like, okay, like, you can't just let the model run bash commands.

1275
00:54:44,810 --> 00:54:46,750
这太不安全了 那你们打算怎么办
Like, that's unsafe. So like, what do you do?

1276
00:54:46,790 --> 00:54:48,030
这根本不是一个能解决的问题
Like, this is not a solvable problem.

1277
00:54:48,070 --> 00:54:49,150
所以我们不能上线这个东西
So like, we can't launch this.

1278
00:54:49,490 --> 00:54:50,830
我就和 Ben Mann 一起头脑风暴
I brainstormed with Ben Mann.

1279
00:54:51,070 --> 00:54:52,930
Ben 是创立实验室团队的人
And Ben was, he started the labs team.

1280
00:54:53,010 --> 00:54:54,490
他也是 Anthropic 的联合创始人之一
He's one of the founders at Anthropic.

1281
